  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Being able to access the point your player is \"looking\" at would be insanely useful for the more inventive applications of constraints and \"world-placement\" avatars.  \n\nIf you could do something like put a drag-and-drop slot in the SDK Avatar component that lets us assign a transform that will go to the raycast target, we'd have a viable cursor for placing \"in-world\" objects better.\n\nOr even just improving the ability for avatars with non-standard dimensions (eg; puppeting a model with a second armature) while still having them look in the correct direction as its gaze converges with the players instead of merely copying in parallel with a rotation constraint.",
